./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v4.md:503:  When `i18n.fallback` is configured, this new routing option controls whether to [redirect](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/routing/#redirects) to the fallback page, or to [rewrite](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/routing/#rewrites) the fallback page's content in place.
./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v4.md:505:  The `"redirect"` option is the default value and matches the current behavior of the existing fallback system.
./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v4.md:979:  Also improves the DX of directing to a new route on success. Actions will now redirect to the route specified in your `action` string on success, and redirect back to the previous page on error. This follows the routing convention of established backend frameworks like Laravel.
./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v4.md:981:  For example, say you want to redirect to a `/success` route when `actions.signup` succeeds. You can add `/success` to your `action` string like so:
./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v4.md:987:  - On success, Astro will redirect to `/success`.
