./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v6.md:11:  The fix replaces the rejection approach with iterative decoding — multi-level percent-encoding is now fully resolved to its canonical form before being passed to middleware and route matching. This preserves the security fix for CVE-2025-66202 (middleware authorization bypass via double encoding) because middleware now always sees the fully decoded path, making bypass impossible. For example, `/api/%2561dmin` is decoded to `/api/admin`, which middleware can correctly block.
