./packages/astro/CHANGELOG-v6.md:383:  Today, Astro handles every incoming request through a fixed internal pipeline: trailing slash normalization, redirects, actions, middleware, page rendering, i18n, and so on. That pipeline works great for most sites, but as projects grow you often want to run your own logic _between_ those steps — an auth check before rendering, a rate limiter before actions, custom logging around the whole stack. Advanced routing gives you that control.
