./build.rs:6:/// Embed a Windows manifest and set some linker options.
./build.rs:7:///
./build.rs:8:/// The main reason for this is to enable long path support on Windows. This
./build.rs:9:/// still, I believe, requires enabling long path support in the registry. But
./build.rs:10:/// if that's enabled, then this will let ripgrep use C:\... style paths that
./build.rs:11:/// are longer than 260 characters.
